# WH-1000XM5 Attach: identification, support functions, battery and noise control.
# Synthesised from libmdr's protocol definitions (MIT, mos9527/SonyHeadphonesClient)
# until a real capture exists; generated by gen.py in this directory. The
# protocol info reply is the XM5 fw 1.1.3 one; the support function list is
# made up but, like the real fw 2.5.1 one, lists battery 0x20 and NC/ASM 0x6b
# (NCASM type 0x17). Battery: 70 %. Noise control: Ambient, Focus on Voice on,
# Ambient Level 10. Then a battery notification of 69 %.
# GET protocol info
2026-10-11T12:00:00.000Z sony >> 3e 0c 00 00 00 00 02 00 00 0e 3c
2026-10-11T12:00:00.010Z sony << 3e 01 01 00 00 00 00 02 3c
2026-10-11T12:00:00.020Z sony << 3e 0c 00 00 00 00 08 01 00 03 00 00 00 00 00 18 3c
2026-10-11T12:00:00.030Z sony >> 3e 01 01 00 00 00 00 02 3c
